   "stem": {
      "text": "Sand is added to and removed from a pile. Let A(t) be the amount of sand in the pile, in tons, at time t hours, for \\( t \\ge 0 \\). The rate of change of A is \\( R(t) = 2 \\sin{\\left(\\frac{t^{2}}{4} \\right)} + 3 \\) tons per hour. At time t = 0, there are 20 tons. Using a calculator, find \\( A(2) \\). Show the setup for the calculation, and give the value correct to three decimal places.",
